  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 200°C/180°C fan-forced. Cut mini flour tortillas into 2cm strips.\n• Finely chop brown onion. Finely grate or crush garlic. Finely grate ginger.\n• Grate carrot (unpeeled). Roughly chop tomato. Pick and roughly chop mint. Drain and rinse lentils.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5f7151aff586ca518e1136bf/step-5a5d14c2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide tortillas between two lined oven trays, arranging in a single layer.\n• Brush (or spray) with olive oil and season.\n• Bake until lightly golden and crisp, 5-7 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5f7151aff586ca518e1136bf/step-0447f6a9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, in a large saucepan, heat butter and a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook onion until softened, 3-4 mins. Add garlic, ginger, Bengal curry paste (see ingredients list) and tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1-2 mins.\n• Add a drizzle more olive oil and add carrot, tomato and lentils. Cook, stirring, until slightly softened, 2-3 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5f7151aff586ca518e1136bf/step-1953e5dd.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Reduce heat to medium and add the salt, water and coconut milk to the pan. Stir to combine.\n• Cook until veggies have softened, 3-4 mins. Add a splash of water if the dhal looks dry.\n• Season and divide between bowls. Top with mint. Serve with flatbread dippers.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5f7151aff586ca518e1136bf/step-5f55cabe.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
